---
/**
 * PressureVolumeLoop — "Loop builder". Three controls (EDV, Ea, Ees) set where a left-ventricular
 * pressure-volume loop's end-systolic corner falls. Model from the lesson's worked problem: linear
 * ESPVR Pes = Ees (ESV - V0) with V0 = 5 mL, Ea = Pes / SV, so SV = (EDV - V0) / (1 + Ea/Ees);
 * ESV = EDV - SV; EF = SV / EDV; CO = SV x 70 per min; SW = SV x mean ejection pressure, where the
 * mean is the average of aortic-opening and end-systolic pressure. The lesson's 80 and 120 mmHg give
 * opening = 2/3 Pes and mean = 5/6 Pes (made up as a rule for the sketch). The EDPVR
 * P = exp(0.02 (V - 5)) - 1 mmHg is invented for the sketch (about 10 mmHg at 125 mL, the lesson's
 * about 10 mmHg at mitral closure). The grey reference loop is the lesson's baseline (EDV 125 mL,
 * Ea 1.5, Ees 3.0). Self-contained vanilla-TS Astro island. Original.
 */
const uid = Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8);
---

<figure class="pvl card" data-pvl>
  <figcaption class="pvl-head">Loop builder: where the end-systolic corner falls<span class="pvl-chip">⚙ original · interactive</span></figcaption>

  <svg class="pvl-svg" viewBox="0 0 340 258" role="img" aria-label="Plot of left ventricular pressure in mmHg against left ventricular volume in mL: a pressure-volume loop run counterclockwise, with the end-systolic pressure-volume line, a curved end-diastolic line and the arterial elastance line" data-plot></svg>

  <ul class="pvl-legend" aria-label="Key to the plot">
    <li><span class="pvl-sw pvl-sw-loop"></span>loop (counterclockwise; shaded area is the area stroke work approximates)</li>
    <li><span class="pvl-sw pvl-sw-espvr"></span>ESPVR, slope Ees</li>
    <li><span class="pvl-sw pvl-sw-edpvr"></span>EDPVR (invented curve for this sketch)</li>
    <li><span class="pvl-sw pvl-sw-ea"></span>Ea line, slope Ea</li>
    <li data-ref-key><span class="pvl-sw pvl-sw-ref"></span>reference loop (the lesson’s baseline)</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="pvl-corners"><b>1</b> mitral closes · <b>2</b> aortic opens · <b>3</b> aortic closes · <b>4</b> mitral opens, then filling along the bottom</p>

  <div class="pvl-controls">
    <label class="pvl-slabel"><span>EDV, preload <em data-out="edv">125</em> mL</span>
      <input type="range" data-in="edv" min="90" max="160" step="5" value="125" />
    </label>
    <label class="pvl-slabel"><span>Ea, afterload <em data-out="ea">1.5</em> mmHg per mL <small>(effective arterial elastance)</small></span>
      <input type="range" data-in="ea" min="1" max="3" step="0.1" value="1.5" />
    </label>
    <label class="pvl-slabel"><span>Ees, an index of contractility <em data-out="ees">3.0</em> mmHg per mL <small>(slope of the ESPVR)</small></span>
      <input type="range" data-in="ees" min="1.5" max="5" step="0.1" value="3" />
    </label>
    <label class="pvl-check"><input type="checkbox" data-in="ref" id={`pvl-ref-${uid}`} checked /> <span>Show reference loop <small>(the lesson’s baseline, in grey)</small></span></label>
    <div class="pvl-marks">Set the sliders to a line of the lesson’s worked problem, part 3:
      <span class="pvl-marklist" data-marks></span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <dl class="pvl-readout">
    <div><dt>Stroke volume, SV = (EDV − V0) / (1 + Ea/Ees)</dt><dd data-r="sv"></dd></div>
    <div><dt>End-systolic volume, ESV = EDV − SV</dt><dd data-r="esv"></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Ejection fraction, EF = SV / EDV</dt><dd data-r="ef"></dd></div>
    <div><dt>End-systolic pressure, Pes = Ea × SV</dt><dd data-r="pes"></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Cardiac output, CO = SV × HR (HR fixed at 70 per min)</dt><dd data-r="co"></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Stroke work ≈ SV × mean ejection pressure (aortic opening taken as 2/3 of Pes in this sketch)</dt><dd data-r="sw"></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Ea/Ees <small>(humans at rest: reported near 0.6)</small></dt><dd data-r="ratio"></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Fixed in this sketch</dt><dd class="pvl-fixed">V0 = 5 mL, HR = 70 per min</dd></div>
  </dl>
  <p class="pvl-why" data-why role="status"></p>

  <p class="pvl-assume">Illustrative model, not fitted to data. In this sketch (made up for the sketch unless the lesson gives it): a model adult left ventricle at rest, steady state, competent valves, linear ESPVR with the lesson’s V0 = 5 mL, heart rate fixed at the lesson’s 70 per min, and Ea held constant as in the lesson’s part 3; the grey reference loop is the lesson’s baseline (EDV 125 mL, Ea 1.5, Ees 3.0 mmHg per mL); the slider ranges are made up; the EDPVR is an invented convex curve, not a measurement, drawn to pass near the lesson’s about 10 mmHg at 125 mL (the lesson says only that the EDPVR is non-linear); aortic opening at 2/3 of Pes and mean ejection pressure at 5/6 of Pes are scaled from the lesson’s 80 and 120 mmHg and are a made-up rule; the top left corner is drawn at Pes, which the lesson rounds to 120 mmHg for simple numbers; the ejection arc is a smooth curve of made-up shape. Readouts use unrounded values. At the extremes of the sliders, pressures and ejection fractions fall far outside the lesson’s examples.</p>

  <p class="pvl-foot">Rule to keep: the end-systolic corner sits where the Ea line, which starts at EDV on the volume axis, meets the ESPVR; preload moves the start of that line, afterload tilts it and contractility tilts the ESPVR, so EF can change without any change in Ees.</p>
</figure>

<script>
  const NS = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
  const ACCENT = '#0e7c86', ORANGE = '#e57200', INK = '#4b4b55', FAINT = '#b9b9c2', GREY = '#8d8d98', PURPLE = '#6a4c93';

  function must<T extends Element>(root: ParentNode, sel: string): T {
    const e = root.querySelector<T>(sel);
    if (!e) throw new Error('PressureVolumeLoop: missing ' + sel);
    return e;
  }
  function el(name: string, attrs: Record<string, string | number>): SVGElement {
    const e = document.createElementNS(NS, name);
    for (const k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, String(attrs[k]));
    return e;
  }
  // number to d decimals, trailing zeros dropped, typographic minus
  const fmt = (x: number, d = 1) => {
    const s = Math.abs(x).toFixed(d);
    const t = s.indexOf('.') >= 0 ? s.replace(/0+$/, '').replace(/\.$/, '') : s;
    return (x < 0 && Number(t) !== 0 ? '−' : '') + t;
  };
  const fmtInt = (x: number) => Math.round(x).toLocaleString('en-US');

  // the lesson's baseline and the four lines of part 3
  const V0 = 5, HR = 70;
  const BASE = { edv: 125, ea: 1.5, ees: 3.0 };
  const ROWS = [
    { label: 'Baseline', edv: 125, ea: 1.5, ees: 3.0 },
    { label: 'Afterload up, Ea 2.0', edv: 125, ea: 2.0, ees: 3.0 },
    { label: 'Preload up, EDV 140', edv: 140, ea: 1.5, ees: 3.0 },
    { label: 'Contractility up, Ees 4.5', edv: 125, ea: 1.5, ees: 4.5 },
  ];

  type S = { edv: number; ea: number; ees: number };
  function solve(s: S) {
    const sv = (s.edv - V0) / (1 + s.ea / s.ees);
    const pes = s.ea * sv;
    const esv = s.edv - sv;
    const ef = sv / s.edv;
    const co = (sv * HR) / 1000; // L per min
    const sw = sv * (5 / 6) * pes; // mmHg mL
    const swJ = sw * 1.333e-4;
    return { sv, pes, esv, ef, co, sw, swJ, ratio: s.ea / s.ees };
  }
  const edpvr = (v: number) => Math.exp(0.02 * (v - V0)) - 1;
  const same = (a: number, b: number) => Math.abs(a - b) < 1e-9;

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-pvl]').forEach((root) => {
    const plot = must<SVGSVGElement>(root, '[data-plot]');
    const edvIn = must<HTMLInputElement>(root, '[data-in="edv"]');
    const eaIn = must<HTMLInputElement>(root, '[data-in="ea"]');
    const eesIn = must<HTMLInputElement>(root, '[data-in="ees"]');
    const refIn = must<HTMLInputElement>(root, '[data-in="ref"]');
    const edvOut = must<HTMLElement>(root, '[data-out="edv"]');
    const eaOut = must<HTMLElement>(root, '[data-out="ea"]');
    const eesOut = must<HTMLElement>(root, '[data-out="ees"]');
    const refKey = must<HTMLElement>(root, '[data-ref-key]');
    const why = must<HTMLElement>(root, '[data-why]');
    const marks = must<HTMLElement>(root, '[data-marks]');
    const rd = (k: string) => must<HTMLElement>(root, `[data-r="${k}"]`);
    const rSv = rd('sv'), rEsv = rd('esv'), rEf = rd('ef'), rPes = rd('pes'), rCo = rd('co'), rSw = rd('sw'), rRatio = rd('ratio');

    // plot geometry (viewBox units)
    const X0 = 44, X1 = 328, Y0 = 22, Y1 = 192, VMAX = 170, PMAX = 300;
    const px = (v: number) => X0 + (v / VMAX) * (X1 - X0);
    const py = (p: number) => Y1 - (p / PMAX) * (Y1 - Y0);

    const buttons: { b: HTMLButtonElement; r: S }[] = [];
    ROWS.forEach((r) => {
      const b = document.createElement('button');
      b.type = 'button';
      b.className = 'pvl-mark';
      b.textContent = r.label;
      b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'false');
      b.addEventListener('click', () => {
        edvIn.value = String(r.edv);
        eaIn.value = String(r.ea);
        eesIn.value = String(r.ees);
        render();
      });
      marks.appendChild(b);
      buttons.push({ b, r });
    });

    // SVG path of one loop: right side up, smooth ejection arc, left side down, filling along the EDPVR
    function loopGeometry(s: S) {
      const m = solve(s);
      const xe = px(s.edv), xs = px(m.esv);
      const yTop = py(m.pes), yOpen = py((2 / 3) * m.pes);
      const yEdp = py(edpvr(s.edv)), yEsEdp = py(edpvr(m.esv));
      const sv = m.sv;
      const c1 = [xe, yOpen], c2 = [px(s.edv - 0.1 * sv), yTop], c3 = [px(m.esv + 0.3 * sv), yTop], c4 = [xs, yTop];
      let d = `M${xe.toFixed(1)} ${yEdp.toFixed(1)} L${xe.toFixed(1)} ${yOpen.toFixed(1)} `;
      d += `C${c2[0].toFixed(1)} ${c2[1].toFixed(1)} ${c3[0].toFixed(1)} ${c3[1].toFixed(1)} ${c4[0].toFixed(1)} ${c4[1].toFixed(1)} `;
      d += `L${xs.toFixed(1)} ${yEsEdp.toFixed(1)} `;
      for (let i = 1; i <= 24; i++) {
        const v = m.esv + (s.edv - m.esv) * (i / 24);
        d += `L${px(v).toFixed(1)} ${py(edpvr(v)).toFixed(1)} `;
      }
      d += 'Z';
      return { d, m, xe, xs, yTop, yOpen, yEdp, yEsEdp, c1, c2, c3, c4 };
    }

    function arrow(x: number, y: number, dx: number, dy: number) {
      const L = Math.hypot(dx, dy) || 1;
      const ux = dx / L, uy = dy / L, nx = -uy, ny = ux;
      const pts = [
        [x + ux * 4.5, y + uy * 4.5],
        [x - ux * 3 + nx * 3.5, y - uy * 3 + ny * 3.5],
        [x - ux * 3 - nx * 3.5, y - uy * 3 - ny * 3.5],
      ];
      return el('polygon', { points: pts.map((p) => p[0].toFixed(1) + ',' + p[1].toFixed(1)).join(' '), fill: ACCENT });
    }

    function badge(x: number, y: number, n: string) {
      const g = el('g', {});
      g.appendChild(el('circle', { cx: x, cy: y, r: 7, fill: '#fff', stroke: ACCENT, 'stroke-width': 1.2 }));
      const t = el('text', { x, y: y + 3.5, 'text-anchor': 'middle', 'font-size': 10, 'font-weight': 700, fill: INK });
      t.textContent = n;
      g.appendChild(t);
      return g;
    }

    function txt(x: number, y: number, s: string, anchor: string, size = 10, extra: Record<string, string | number> = {}) {
      const t = el('text', { x, y, 'text-anchor': anchor, 'font-size': size, fill: INK, ...extra });
      t.textContent = s;
      return t;
    }

    function render() {
      const s: S = { edv: parseFloat(edvIn.value), ea: parseFloat(eaIn.value), ees: parseFloat(eesIn.value) };
      const showRef = refIn.checked;
      edvOut.textContent = fmt(s.edv, 0);
      eaOut.textContent = s.ea.toFixed(1);
      eesOut.textContent = s.ees.toFixed(1);
      refKey.hidden = !showRef;

      const g = loopGeometry(s);
      const m = g.m;
      const b = solve(BASE);

      plot.replaceChildren();
      // axes and ticks
      plot.appendChild(el('line', { x1: X0, y1: Y0 - 4, x2: X0, y2: Y1, stroke: INK, 'stroke-width': 1 }));
      plot.appendChild(el('line', { x1: X0, y1: Y1, x2: X1, y2: Y1, stroke: INK, 'stroke-width': 1 }));
      for (const p of [0, 100, 200, 300]) {
        plot.appendChild(el('line', { x1: X0 - 3, y1: py(p), x2: X0, y2: py(p), stroke: INK, 'stroke-width': 1 }));
        if (p > 0) plot.appendChild(el('line', { x1: X0, y1: py(p), x2: X1, y2: py(p), stroke: FAINT, 'stroke-width': 0.6, 'stroke-dasharray': '2 3' }));
        plot.appendChild(txt(X0 - 5, py(p) + 3.5, String(p), 'end', 9));
      }
      for (const v of [0, 50, 100, 150]) {
        plot.appendChild(el('line', { x1: px(v), y1: Y1, x2: px(v), y2: Y1 + 3, stroke: INK, 'stroke-width': 1 }));
        plot.appendChild(txt(px(v), Y1 + 13, String(v), 'middle', 9));
      }
      plot.appendChild(txt(X0 + 4, 12, 'LV pressure (mmHg)', 'start', 10));
      plot.appendChild(txt(X1, 12, 'in this sketch', 'end', 10, { 'font-style': 'italic' }));
      plot.appendChild(txt((X0 + X1) / 2, Y1 + 52, 'LV volume (mL)', 'middle', 10));

      // EDPVR curve (illustrative)
      let ed = '';
      for (let v = V0; v <= VMAX; v += 5) ed += (v === V0 ? 'M' : 'L') + px(v).toFixed(1) + ' ' + py(Math.min(edpvr(v), PMAX)).toFixed(1) + ' ';
      plot.appendChild(el('path', { d: ed.trim(), fill: 'none', stroke: PURPLE, 'stroke-width': 1.3 }));

      // ESPVR line: from V0 on the volume axis, clipped at the plot's top or right edge
      const vEnd = Math.min(VMAX, V0 + PMAX / s.ees);
      plot.appendChild(el('line', { x1: px(V0), y1: py(0), x2: px(vEnd), y2: py(s.ees * (vEnd - V0)), stroke: INK, 'stroke-width': 1.4 }));

      // reference loop in grey (the lesson's baseline)
      if (showRef) {
        const gr = loopGeometry(BASE);
        plot.appendChild(el('path', { d: gr.d, fill: 'none', stroke: GREY, 'stroke-width': 1.6, 'stroke-dasharray': '4 3' }));
      }

      // Ea line: from (EDV, 0) to the end-systolic corner
      plot.appendChild(el('line', { x1: px(s.edv), y1: py(0), x2: g.xs, y2: g.yTop, stroke: ORANGE, 'stroke-width': 1.6, 'stroke-dasharray': '5 3' }));

      // current loop: shaded area and outline
      plot.appendChild(el('path', { d: g.d, fill: ACCENT, 'fill-opacity': 0.14, stroke: ACCENT, 'stroke-width': 2.4, 'stroke-linejoin': 'round' }));

      // direction arrows (counterclockwise): up the right side, left along the top, down the left side, right along the bottom
      plot.appendChild(arrow(g.xe, (g.yEdp + g.yOpen) / 2, 0, -1));
      {
        const t = 0.5, u = 1 - t;
        const bx = u * u * u * g.c1[0] + 3 * u * u * t * g.c2[0] + 3 * u * t * t * g.c3[0] + t * t * t * g.c4[0];
        const by = u * u * u * g.c1[1] + 3 * u * u * t * g.c2[1] + 3 * u * t * t * g.c3[1] + t * t * t * g.c4[1];
        const dx = 3 * u * u * (g.c2[0] - g.c1[0]) + 6 * u * t * (g.c3[0] - g.c2[0]) + 3 * t * t * (g.c4[0] - g.c3[0]);
        const dy = 3 * u * u * (g.c2[1] - g.c1[1]) + 6 * u * t * (g.c3[1] - g.c2[1]) + 3 * t * t * (g.c4[1] - g.c3[1]);
        plot.appendChild(arrow(bx, by, dx, dy));
      }
      plot.appendChild(arrow(g.xs, (g.yTop + g.yEsEdp) / 2, 0, 1));
      {
        const vm = (m.esv + s.edv) / 2;
        plot.appendChild(arrow(px(vm), py(edpvr(vm)), px(vm + 1) - px(vm), py(edpvr(vm + 1)) - py(edpvr(vm))));
      }

      // corner dots and numbered badges (1 mitral closes, 2 aortic opens, 3 aortic closes, 4 mitral opens)
      const corners: [number, number][] = [[g.xe, g.yEdp], [g.xe, g.yOpen], [g.xs, g.yTop], [g.xs, g.yEsEdp]];
      corners.forEach((c) => plot.appendChild(el('circle', { cx: c[0], cy: c[1], r: 2.8, fill: ACCENT })));
      plot.appendChild(badge(g.xe + 11, g.yEdp - 2, '1'));
      plot.appendChild(badge(g.xe + 11, g.yOpen, '2'));
      plot.appendChild(badge(g.xs - 11, g.yTop, '3'));
      plot.appendChild(badge(g.xs - 11, g.yEsEdp - 2, '4'));

      // stroke-volume bar under the axis, with EDV and ESV drop lines
      const yb = Y1 + 27;
      plot.appendChild(el('line', { x1: g.xs, y1: Y1, x2: g.xs, y2: yb + 3, stroke: ACCENT, 'stroke-width': 1, 'stroke-dasharray': '2 2' }));
      plot.appendChild(el('line', { x1: g.xe, y1: Y1, x2: g.xe, y2: yb + 3, stroke: ACCENT, 'stroke-width': 1, 'stroke-dasharray': '2 2' }));
      plot.appendChild(el('line', { x1: g.xs, y1: yb, x2: g.xe, y2: yb, stroke: ACCENT, 'stroke-width': 1.6 }));
      plot.appendChild(txt((g.xs + g.xe) / 2, yb + 11, 'SV ' + fmt(m.sv) + ' mL', 'middle', 10, { 'font-weight': 700 }));

      // readouts
      rSv.textContent = fmt(m.sv) + ' mL';
      rEsv.textContent = fmt(m.esv) + ' mL';
      rEf.textContent = fmt(m.ef * 100) + ' percent';
      rPes.textContent = fmt(m.pes) + ' mmHg';
      rCo.textContent = fmt(m.co, 2) + ' L per min';
      rSw.textContent = fmtInt(m.sw) + ' mmHg mL = ' + fmt(m.swJ, 2) + ' J per beat';
      rRatio.textContent = m.ratio.toFixed(2);

      // preset buttons
      buttons.forEach(({ b: btn, r }) => btn.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(same(r.edv, s.edv) && same(r.ea, s.ea) && same(r.ees, s.ees))));

      // status sentence: every sentence is a result of this sketch's arithmetic
      const dir = (now: number, was: number, up: string, down: string, eq: string) => (same(now, was) ? eq : now > was ? up : down);
      const changed = [!same(s.edv, BASE.edv), !same(s.ea, BASE.ea), !same(s.ees, BASE.ees)].filter(Boolean).length;
      const eqn = `In this sketch, SV = (EDV − V0) / (1 + Ea/Ees) = ${fmt(s.edv - V0)} / (1 + ${fmt(m.ratio, 3)}) = ${fmt(m.sv)} mL, so ESV = ${fmt(m.esv)} mL and Pes = Ea × SV = ${fmt(m.pes)} mmHg, the point where the Ea line meets the ESPVR.`;
      let more: string;
      if (changed === 0) {
        more = `This is the lesson’s baseline loop, with Ea/Ees = ${m.ratio.toFixed(2)}, which the lesson calls near the efficiency optimum that models predict.`;
      } else if (changed > 1) {
        more = `In this sketch, more than one control differs from the baseline, so their effects combine. Against the baseline, SV is ${dir(m.sv, b.sv, 'higher', 'lower', 'the same')} (${fmt(m.sv)} against ${fmt(b.sv)} mL), ESV is ${dir(m.esv, b.esv, 'higher', 'lower', 'the same')} (${fmt(m.esv)} against ${fmt(b.esv)} mL) and Pes is ${dir(m.pes, b.pes, 'higher', 'lower', 'the same')} (${fmt(m.pes)} against ${fmt(b.pes)} mmHg).`;
      } else if (!same(s.ea, BASE.ea)) {
        const up = s.ea > BASE.ea;
        more = up
          ? `In this sketch, higher afterload steepens the Ea line, which meets the same ESPVR at a higher pressure and a larger volume: ESV rises, SV falls and EF falls (${fmt(m.ef * 100)} against ${fmt(b.ef * 100)} percent) with Ees unchanged.`
          : `In this sketch, lower afterload flattens the Ea line, which meets the same ESPVR at a lower pressure and a smaller volume: ESV falls, SV rises and EF rises (${fmt(m.ef * 100)} against ${fmt(b.ef * 100)} percent) with Ees unchanged.`;
      } else if (!same(s.edv, BASE.edv)) {
        const up = s.edv > BASE.edv;
        const dsv = Math.abs(m.sv - b.sv), dedv = Math.abs(s.edv - BASE.edv);
        more = up
          ? `In this sketch, higher preload slides the end-systolic corner up the same ESPVR: SV rises by ${fmt(dsv)} mL, less than the ${fmt(dedv)} mL rise in EDV, because Pes rises too (${fmt(m.pes)} against ${fmt(b.pes)} mmHg).`
          : `In this sketch, lower preload slides the end-systolic corner down the same ESPVR: SV falls by ${fmt(dsv)} mL, less than the ${fmt(dedv)} mL fall in EDV, because Pes falls too (${fmt(m.pes)} against ${fmt(b.pes)} mmHg).`;
      } else {
        const up = s.ees > BASE.ees;
        more = up
          ? `In this sketch, higher Ees steepens the ESPVR and lowers ESV (${fmt(m.esv)} against ${fmt(b.esv)} mL); SV and EF rise (EF ${fmt(m.ef * 100)} against ${fmt(b.ef * 100)} percent) with EDV and Ea unchanged.`
          : `In this sketch, lower Ees flattens the ESPVR and raises ESV (${fmt(m.esv)} against ${fmt(b.esv)} mL); SV and EF fall (EF ${fmt(m.ef * 100)} against ${fmt(b.ef * 100)} percent) with EDV and Ea unchanged.`;
      }
      why.textContent = eqn + ' ' + more;
    }

    [edvIn, eaIn, eesIn, refIn].forEach((c) => c.addEventListener('input', render));
    refIn.addEventListener('change', render);
    render();
  });
</script>

<style is:global>
  .pvl { padding: var(--ddp-space-3) var(--ddp-space-4) var(--ddp-space-4); margin: var(--ddp-space-5) 0; }
  .pvl-head { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 0.3rem; font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--ddp-text-sm); color: var(--ddp-color-primary); margin-bottom: var(--ddp-space-3); }
  .pvl-chip { font-family: var(--ddp-font-mono); font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); font-weight: 400; color: var(--ddp-color-muted); }
